---
description: Interaction and UI rules for the active workout experience, glass styling, and Dynamic Island
alwaysApply: true
---

- Prioritize logging speed over visual flourish.
- The active workout screen should be built around exercise cards with set rows.
- Use inline editing for set values.
- Do not use modals for normal set edits.
- One tap should complete a set.
- Add Set should clone the prior set when possible.
- Keep the timer visible and lightweight.
- Use glass/material effects only on structural containers such as:
  - top header
  - summary strip
  - timer bar
  - sheets
  - tab/navigation chrome
- Use solid, crisp surfaces for set rows and numeric input cells.
- Dynamic Island and Live Activity should show only glanceable data:
  - elapsed workout time
  - current exercise name
  - active rest countdown
  - optionally completed set count
